course: dictionary
lesson: 13696
title: Animals that eat insects
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An insectivore is an animal or plant that eats mainly insects. Look at the word in two parts: insect and -vore. The ending -vore means eater, so an insectivore is an insect eater.
explain: Other words follow the same pattern. A herbivore eats plants, a carnivore eats meat, and an omnivore eats both. «The frog is an insectivore, so it catches flies with its long, sticky tongue.» The clue is in the word itself: insect- tells you what it eats.
explain: Plants can be insectivores too. «The Venus flytrap is an insectivore: it snaps shut when a fly lands on its leaves.» A plant that traps insects is called an insectivorous plant, and it eats them to get the nutrients it needs from its food.
explain: Science has an older meaning too. Long ago, scientists used insectivore for a group of small mammals such as shrews, moles and hedgehogs. Today we use the word mainly for what an animal eats, so when you read it, check whether the text is about diet or about that old group.
fact: Insectivore comes from insect and -vore, which means eater.
fact: Other diet words: herbivore (plants), carnivore (meat), omnivore (both plants and meat).
fact: Examples of insectivores include anteaters, bats, swallows, frogs and hedgehogs.
fact: Venus flytraps are insectivorous plants: they catch insects and eat them.
fact: In older science, insectivore was a group name for small mammals like shrews, moles and hedgehogs.
exercise: «The swallow is an insectivore that catches flies in the air.» What does insectivore mean? | An animal that eats only meat | An animal that lives in the sea | *An animal or plant that eats mainly insects | A plant that grows in the sunlight
exercise: Which word means an animal that eats only plants? | Carnivore | *Herbivore | Omnivore | Insectivore
exercise: Which animal is an insectivore? | A rabbit, which eats carrots | *A bat, which catches moths in the dark | A cow, which eats grass | A lion, which hunts zebras
test: Which word means an animal that eats both plants and meat? | Carnivore | Herbivore | Insectivore | *Omnivore
test: Which of these is a word that, in older science, meant a group of small mammals like shrews and moles? | Herbivore | Reptile | Carnivore | *Insectivore
exam: Which sentence uses insectivore correctly? | «The insectivore drank a cup of tea.» | «The hedgehog is an insectivore, so it snuffles around the garden for beetles.» | «The insectivore is a loud, shiny car.» | *«The hedgehog is an insectivore, so it snuffles around the garden for beetles and caterpillars.»
